<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Try the AI Contact Centre (Council Reception)</h1>

<div class="govuk-panel govuk-panel--confirmation ndx-walkthrough-value-prop">
  <h2 class="govuk-panel__title">
    23 minutes to dial a real council and watch one case capture both your call and your photo
  </h2>
  <div class="govuk-panel__body">
    Call a real UK number from your own phone. Walk a happy-path script. Send a photo through the in-browser photo upload simulator. Then dial back and hear the bot read: "I've reviewed your photo; environmental health will visit Wednesday, ref ABC123."
  </div>
</div>

<div class="govuk-inset-text ndx-walkthrough-reassurance">
  <strong class="govuk-!-font-size-24">No technical knowledge required</strong>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    This walkthrough guides you through a working AI contact centre as a resident would experience it. You will dial a real phone number, send a photo, and watch one case form across both channels. Perfect for council CIOs, customer services directors, contact centre managers, and anyone evaluating AI for resident-facing services.
  </p>
</div>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Your sandbox provisions a full Amazon Connect contact centre with a real UK phone number you call from your own mobile or landline. It includes a Lex bot, a Bedrock Knowledge Base with Guardrails, a multi-intent decomposer, multimodal photo description, Connect Cases, Customer Profiles, and Contact Lens with PII redaction. A companion web app lets you watch the live transcript, the case being built, and the photo upload simulator side by side.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What you'll do</h2>

<p class="govuk-body-l">In this 23-minute walkthrough, you'll:</p>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li><strong>Dial in</strong>, call the real UK number from your own phone, walk a happy-path bin-collection script, and hear the bot read back a reference number (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>Try a multi-intent distressed call</strong>, play a layered script that mentions five different issues, and watch the bot triage the top four (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>Send a photo</strong>, attach a photo using the in-browser photo upload simulator and watch the bot describe it (4 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>One case, two channels (the headline moment)</strong>, dial back and hear the bot link your call and your photo to a single case (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>Inspect sentiment and safeguarding</strong>, look at the redacted transcript and the safeguarding flag (4 minutes)</li>
</ol>

<div class="ndx-walkthrough-prerequisites">
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Before you start</h2>

  <div class="govuk-warning-text">
    <span class="govuk-warning-text__icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
    <strong class="govuk-warning-text__text">
      <span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Important</span>
      You must have already requested the AI Contact Centre scenario via NDX:Try and enabled Bedrock model access for amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0 and amazon.nova-pro-v1:0.
    </strong>
  </div>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a href="/scenarios/ai-contact-centre/" class="govuk-link">Deploy the AI Contact Centre scenario</a> if you haven't already. Deployment takes 30 to 60 minutes; Bedrock Knowledge Base ingestion is the long pole. You'll also need a working phone to dial the number in Step 1.
  </p>
</div>

